  "notes": "Bijan Saadat’s architectural survey, quoted by Seyyed Abdollah Anwar, records a 31.20 m apex and 16.40 m gold-covered zone. Early 1911 exterior plates establish the rounded gold silhouette, four iwans, arcaded walls, narrow golden minaret profile and multi-level kettle-drum pavilion. The publicly documented northwest clock and northeastern iwan establish the surviving court arrangement."
